.TH WAYDROID-REBOOT-PATCH 1 "2026-10-30" "1.0.0" "waydroid-reboot-patch"
.SH NAME
waydroid-reboot-patch \- fix Waydroid closing after Android reboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B waydroid-reboot-patch
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
Patches two files in the
.B waydroid
package to fix a race condition where an in-guest Android reboot causes the
LXC container to fail restarting within the hard 10-second window, killing
.B waydroid-container.service
and leaving Waydroid unresponsive.

A pacman alpm hook automatically re-applies the patches whenever
.B waydroid
is upgraded.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Apply all patches (idempotent).
.TP
.B check
Report which patches are currently applied.
.TP
.B remove
Restore original waydroid files via pacman and remove the systemd drop-in.
.SH PATCHES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/waydroid/tools/services/hardware_manager.py
Wraps
.B reboot()
and the reboot branch of
.B shutdownRequest()
in a 3-attempt retry loop with 5-second gaps.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/waydroid/tools/helpers/lxc.py
Extends
.B wait_for_running()
timeout from 10 to 30 seconds so the container has time to reach RUNNING
after binder node reset.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/waydroid-container.service.d/restart.conf
Adds
.B Restart=on-failure
as a backstop in case the service still exits unexpectedly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR waydroid (1),
.BR lxc-start (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Patch authored against waydroid 1.6.3.
